<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>Astres: Obtention of the Sun azimuth and elevation in a place, date and hour on the Earth</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
 <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
  <p>The azimuth is given in degrees with respect to the North and clockwise; for example, 90° indicates that the Sun is in the Est.<br/>
  The elevation is given in degrees with respect to the horizontal; for example, 90° indicates that the Sun is at the zenith. </p>

  <p>In command line (Astres), angular units introduced in the program must be expressed in degrees, NOT in degrees, minuts and seconds; 
  for example 70° 30' should be expressed as 70.5. Although, in Windows interface (wAstres) you have two possibilities; if you choose degrees, 
  the value with decimals  should be indicated at longitude and latitude boxes.</p>

  <p> Months are expressed as 1-12 (January-December) and  days as 1-31.</p>
  
  <p> Time is expressed in hours; 10:45 is indicated 10.75. Local solar time is considered by default, but it can be in UTC if the
  <i>/UTC</i> parameter is indicated.</p>

  <p>The author is specially grateful to Dr. Josep Girbau, from the Universitat Autònoma de Barcelona, for his help in the writing of this program.</p>
  <hr/>

  <exclusiva>
   <!-- Aquí inicia la part corresponent a la sintaxi de miramon. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpssintaxi"/>
<!-- Aquí acaba la part corresponent a la sintaxi de miramon editable de el WPS.-->
    <p>Example for the (Barcelona) in March 27th of 1999 at 10:45 am:<br/>
    Astres 2.116944 41.42416667 27 3 1999 10.75</p>
<p><!-- $$EXCLUSIVA$$

To obtain the complete help, please type:
Astres ?
--></p>
  </exclusiva>
</body>
</html>